**env activation**
- pyenv activate payroll-env


**Models:**
- `Employee` — profile, government IDs, salary
- `Attendance` — date, time in/out, status
- `LeaveRequest` — type, dates, approval status
- `PayrollRun` — period, status (draft/review/approved/paid/locked)
- `Payslip` — employee, run, gross, deductions breakdown, net
- `DeductionTable` — versioned SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG/tax brackets

---

## Key Decisions

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| **Django Groups for roles** (not User subclasses) | Roles are permissions, not types. Avoids migration pain. |
| **JWT auth** | React SPA + separate backend = simplest. |
| **Deduction tables in DB** (not hardcoded) | Laws change; old payrolls must stay valid. Insert new row = done. |
| **Pure Python calculation engine** | Testable against official calculators before any UI work. |
| **Soft-delete on payroll records** | Legally auditable. Never `DELETE`. |
| **Lock after approval** | Prevents edits to finalized payroll. |

---

## Critical Rules

1. **Never delete payroll records** — soft-delete only.
2. **Lock payroll runs after approval** — no edits allowed.
3. **Audit log every payroll action** (who, what, when).
4. **Encrypt sensitive fields** (TIN, bank account, SSS number) at rest.
5. **Backup the database daily.**
6. **Version deduction tables** — never hardcode rates in views/models.
7. **Calculation engine must be fully tested** before any UI work.

---

## Build Order

| Phase | Deliverable |
|---|---|
| 1 | Project setup (Django + DRF + React + JWT + CORS) |
| 2 | Employee model + CRUD API |
| 3 | Attendance model + CRUD |
| 4 | **Calculation engine (pure Python, unit tested)** |
| 5 | PayrollRun + Payslip compute endpoint |
| 6 | Payslip PDF generation |
| 7 | BIR 1601-C & SSS CCL exports |
| 8 | React pages (login → dashboard → payroll) |
| 9 | Roles & permissions |
| 10 | Deploy + daily backup |

> ⚠️ **Do not skip Phase 4.** If the engine is wrong, nothing else matters.

---

## Tech Stack

- **Backend:** Django 4.2 LTS, DRF, SimpleJWT, django-cors-headers, django-filter
- **PDF:** WeasyPrint
- **Excel export:** openpyxl
- **Frontend:** React 18 + Vite + TailwindCSS + React Router + Axios
- **Database:** SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod)
- **Python:** 3.10+ via pyenv